[{:db/id "841dff1d-35b4-5aa5-8546-c8d913c38da8" :answer/id #uuid "841dff1d-35b4-5aa5-8546-c8d913c38da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 8)(x + 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d3c6aa70-6d67-5a46-a185-c447bb5eb7a9" :answer/id #uuid "d3c6aa70-6d67-5a46-a185-c447bb5eb7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 2)(x + 8)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "118ff845-c36f-5dd4-b4be-4d2f3371534c" :answer/id #uuid "118ff845-c36f-5dd4-b4be-4d2f3371534c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 2)(3 - x)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b5ae0968-bc81-5c09-a845-ff58e0c7403c" :answer/id #uuid "b5ae0968-bc81-5c09-a845-ff58e0c7403c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3 - x)(x + 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "78bfce02-698c-5299-8a19-d1bf108af9a1" :answer/id #uuid "78bfce02-698c-5299-8a19-d1bf108af9a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 3)(x + 8)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bd4776a5-a31b-5b77-b1f4-5f3410bc9a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4776a5-a31b-5b77-b1f4-5f3410bc9a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["841dff1d-35b4-5aa5-8546-c8d913c38da8" "d3c6aa70-6d67-5a46-a185-c447bb5eb7a9" "118ff845-c36f-5dd4-b4be-4d2f3371534c" "b5ae0968-bc81-5c09-a845-ff58e0c7403c" "78bfce02-698c-5299-8a19-d1bf108af9a1"] :answer-field/correct "d3c6aa70-6d67-5a46-a185-c447bb5eb7a9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "6cc14d2b-da71-5a68-9167-1fb9cf53907c" :question/id #uuid "6cc14d2b-da71-5a68-9167-1fb9cf53907c" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48=(x - 3)(x - 1)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=x^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48.$ We know that $(x - 3)$ and $(x - 1)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x - 3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x - 3)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x - 3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | $x^{4}$ | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-37$ | $82$ | $-48$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $3$ | $15$ | $-66$ | $48$ |\n|  | $1$ | $5$ | $-22$ | $16$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48}{x - 3}=x^{3} + 5 x^{2} - 22 x + 16,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48=(x - 3)(x^{3} + 5 x^{2} - 22 x + 16).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x - 1)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(x^{3} + 5 x^{2} - 22 x + 16).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x - 1)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $5$ | $-22$ | $16$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $1$ | $6$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $6$ | $-16$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^{3} + 5 x^{2} - 22 x + 16}{x - 1}=x^{2} + 6 x - 16,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48=(x - 3)(x - 1)(x^{2} + 6 x - 16).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 2 x^{3} - 37 x^{2} + 82 x - 48=(x - 3)(x - 1)\\underbrace{(x - 2)(x + 8)}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(x - 2)(x + 8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["bd4776a5-a31b-5b77-b1f4-5f3410bc9a46"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "2a8f4cd9-343f-53f9-8da8-6987fb92aa94" :answer/id #uuid "2a8f4cd9-343f-53f9-8da8-6987fb92aa94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 2)(x + 4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e5b189d5-4fe1-5252-a78f-94a54754ba0a" :answer/id #uuid "e5b189d5-4fe1-5252-a78f-94a54754ba0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x + 2)(x + 4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3b5c0465-6f7c-51a9-b3cb-19ece0fb2e97" :answer/id #uuid "3b5c0465-6f7c-51a9-b3cb-19ece0fb2e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x + 2)(x - 4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5f60ea94-d78d-524d-860b-1089e09972ec" :answer/id #uuid "5f60ea94-d78d-524d-860b-1089e09972ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x - 2)(x - 4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "eef6d77e-1cb5-5f09-87d0-24953d96ba59" :answer/id #uuid "eef6d77e-1cb5-5f09-87d0-24953d96ba59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2 - x)(x + 4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8a9a23eb-f99e-5776-9814-77b6f94072b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9a23eb-f99e-5776-9814-77b6f94072b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["2a8f4cd9-343f-53f9-8da8-6987fb92aa94" "e5b189d5-4fe1-5252-a78f-94a54754ba0a" "3b5c0465-6f7c-51a9-b3cb-19ece0fb2e97" "5f60ea94-d78d-524d-860b-1089e09972ec" "eef6d77e-1cb5-5f09-87d0-24953d96ba59"] :answer-field/correct "e5b189d5-4fe1-5252-a78f-94a54754ba0a" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "996d568b-7577-52b3-ac06-045db9647695" :question/id #uuid "996d568b-7577-52b3-ac06-045db9647695" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96=(x + 4)(x + 3)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=x^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96.$ We know that $(x + 4)$ and $(x + 3)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x + 3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x + 3)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x + 3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | $x^{4}$ | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $13$ | $62$ | $128$ | $96$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $-3$ | $-30$ | $-96$ | $-96$ |\n|  | $1$ | $10$ | $32$ | $32$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96}{x + 3}=x^{3} + 10 x^{2} + 32 x + 32,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96=(x + 3)(x^{3} + 10 x^{2} + 32 x + 32).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x + 4)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(x^{3} + 10 x^{2} + 32 x + 32).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x + 4)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $10$ | $32$ | $32$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $-4$ | $-24$ | $-32$ |\n|  | $1$ | $6$ | $8$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^{3} + 10 x^{2} + 32 x + 32}{x + 4}=x^{2} + 6 x + 8,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96=(x + 4)(x + 3)(x^{2} + 6 x + 8).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\nx^{4} + 13 x^{3} + 62 x^{2} + 128 x + 96=(x + 4)(x + 3)\\underbrace{(x + 2)(x + 4)}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(x + 2)(x + 4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["8a9a23eb-f99e-5776-9814-77b6f94072b8"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "263727d6-d29d-5bf3-b0ce-64f4c4babbe0" :answer/id #uuid "263727d6-d29d-5bf3-b0ce-64f4c4babbe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4 x - 2)(x)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cf48ea9f-6f25-5c77-b923-06e53622bb21" :answer/id #uuid "cf48ea9f-6f25-5c77-b923-06e53622bb21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3 x + 2)(x - 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "34dd07d8-0fb5-5860-b429-c5d95674c1e6" :answer/id #uuid "34dd07d8-0fb5-5860-b429-c5d95674c1e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2 x + 2)(x + 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9c538ed4-e63a-59ea-b5d7-1bf260ff251e" :answer/id #uuid "9c538ed4-e63a-59ea-b5d7-1bf260ff251e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2 x - 2)(x + 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "632410d0-6cb4-56f4-acbe-ce18db1f0810" :answer/id #uuid "632410d0-6cb4-56f4-acbe-ce18db1f0810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3 x - 2)(x - 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4c1f5d50-c28c-5707-9506-4115f417afd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1f5d50-c28c-5707-9506-4115f417afd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["263727d6-d29d-5bf3-b0ce-64f4c4babbe0" "cf48ea9f-6f25-5c77-b923-06e53622bb21" "34dd07d8-0fb5-5860-b429-c5d95674c1e6" "9c538ed4-e63a-59ea-b5d7-1bf260ff251e" "632410d0-6cb4-56f4-acbe-ce18db1f0810"] :answer-field/correct "632410d0-6cb4-56f4-acbe-ce18db1f0810" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0419dbc0-1445-5bc9-b917-8b83592d2040" :question/id #uuid "0419dbc0-1445-5bc9-b917-8b83592d2040" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4=(x - 2)(x - 1)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4.$ We know that $(x - 2)$ and $(x - 1)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x - 2)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x - 2)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x - 2)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | $x^{4}$ | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $3$ | $-14$ | $23$ | $-16$ | $4$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $-16$ | $14$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-8$ | $7$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4}{x - 2}=3 x^{3} - 8 x^{2} + 7 x - 2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4=(x - 2)(3 x^{3} - 8 x^{2} + 7 x - 2).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x - 1)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(3 x^{3} - 8 x^{2} + 7 x - 2).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x - 1)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-8$ | $7$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $3$ | $-5$ | $2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-5$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 x^{3} - 8 x^{2} + 7 x - 2}{x - 1}=3 x^{2} - 5 x + 2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4=(x - 2)(x - 1)(3 x^{2} - 5 x + 2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 14 x^{3} + 23 x^{2} - 16 x + 4=(x - 2)(x - 1)\\underbrace{(3 x - 2)(x - 1)}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(3 x - 2)(x - 1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["4c1f5d50-c28c-5707-9506-4115f417afd9"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8f11b303-bb92-5db1-95e6-fc4409a201ad" :answer/id #uuid "8f11b303-bb92-5db1-95e6-fc4409a201ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2 x + 2)(x - 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c8e6fe5f-e80f-5c47-9d4c-f222856f886d" :answer/id #uuid "c8e6fe5f-e80f-5c47-9d4c-f222856f886d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3 x - 1)(x + 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c4ee89c0-7563-5d3c-aabb-4556e6f4b071" :answer/id #uuid "c4ee89c0-7563-5d3c-aabb-4556e6f4b071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2 x - 2)(x - 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "99dac682-5f1b-579c-8e61-9f4cda6acd23" :answer/id #uuid "99dac682-5f1b-579c-8e61-9f4cda6acd23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3 x + 1)(x + 2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4a850ce8-6c2f-56e9-97a6-d54695d622f9" :answer/id #uuid "4a850ce8-6c2f-56e9-97a6-d54695d622f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4 x - 2)(x + 3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b57ab9bd-7e2d-5b40-9052-da97505a6cff" :answer-field/id #uuid "b57ab9bd-7e2d-5b40-9052-da97505a6cff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8f11b303-bb92-5db1-95e6-fc4409a201ad" "c8e6fe5f-e80f-5c47-9d4c-f222856f886d" "c4ee89c0-7563-5d3c-aabb-4556e6f4b071" "99dac682-5f1b-579c-8e61-9f4cda6acd23" "4a850ce8-6c2f-56e9-97a6-d54695d622f9"] :answer-field/correct "c8e6fe5f-e80f-5c47-9d4c-f222856f886d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "de6b8b43-d602-5cd2-be14-bed17971288f" :question/id #uuid "de6b8b43-d602-5cd2-be14-bed17971288f" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6=(x - 1)(x - 3)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6.$ We know that $(x - 1)$ and $(x - 3)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x - 1)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x - 1)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x - 1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | $x^{4}$ | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $-13$ | $23$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $-17$ | $6$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $-17$ | $6$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6}{x - 1}=3 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} - 17 x + 6,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6=(x - 1)(3 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} - 17 x + 6).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x - 3)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(3 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} - 17 x + 6).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x - 3)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | $x^{3}$ | $x^{2}$ | $x^{1}$ | $x^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $-17$ | $6$ |\n|  | $\\downarrow$ | $9$ | $15$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $3$ | $5$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} - 17 x + 6}{x - 3}=3 x^{2} + 5 x - 2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6=(x - 1)(x - 3)(3 x^{2} + 5 x - 2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n3 x^{4} - 7 x^{3} - 13 x^{2} + 23 x - 6=(x - 1)(x - 3)\\underbrace{(3 x - 1)(x + 2)}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(3 x - 1)(x + 2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["b57ab9bd-7e2d-5b40-9052-da97505a6cff"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9901435b-c59a-5204-b93c-abef284df7ad" :answer/id #uuid "9901435b-c59a-5204-b93c-abef284df7ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4 x - 2)(x - 1)" :db/ensure :answer/v